            "body": "## Code Review\n\nThis pull request addresses two issues: it improves a misleading error message for cancellation requests on completed responses and reduces log noise by changing an error-level log for intentional cancellations to a debug-level log. The changes are correct and beneficial. I've added one comment to further improve the robustness of the cancellation logic by handling cases where the background task might fail with an exception other than `CancelledError` during the cancellation process, which would prevent the `cancel` endpoint from returning a 500 error.",
            "comments": {
              "nodes": [
                {
                  "author": {
                    "__typename": "Bot",
                    "login": "gemini-code-assist"
                  },
                  "body": "![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)\n\nThe `await task` call after `task.cancel()` can raise exceptions other than `asyncio.CancelledError` if the task fails for another reason before it is cancelled. This would cause an unhandled exception in `cancel_responses`, leading to a 500 error for the client. To make this endpoint more robust, it's best to also handle other exceptions that might arise from awaiting the task.\n\nThe background task runner (`_run_background_request`) is already responsible for handling task failures, logging them, and updating the response status. Therefore, we can catch any exception here and log it at a debug level to prevent the `cancel` endpoint from crashing.\n\n```suggestion\n            try:\n                await task\n            except asyncio.CancelledError:\n                logger.debug(\"Background task for %s was cancelled\", response_id)\n            except Exception:\n                logger.debug(\"Task for %s failed during cancellation\", response_id)\n```",
                  "createdAt": "2026-03-01T15:46:31Z",
                  "databaseId": 2869265051,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -1252,7 +1252,7 @@ async def cancel_responses(\n             try:\n                 await task\n             except asyncio.CancelledError:\n-                logger.exception(\"Background task for %s was cancelled\", response_id)\n+                logger.debug(\"Background task for %s was cancelled\", response_id)",
                  "line": 1321,
                  "originalLine": 1255,
                  "path": "vllm/entrypoints/openai/responses/serving.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-03-01T15:46:32Z",
